UID:94413-1789758000-1789763400@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Swar\, Soch\, Laya
DESCRIPTION:Music begins where words end. \nThis evening of Hindustani classical music explores the intimate connection between thought\, emotion and musical expression. Through vocals and tabla\, the unspoken nuances of the inner mind are expressed through raga\, swara\, alaap and laya. \nThe evening features a vocal recital by Mandakini\, exploring the depth\, beauty and emotional dimensions of the raga through meditative expanse and rhythmic interplay. It also features a solo tabla presentation by Kaustuv\, showcasing the expressive vocabulary of tabla in the traditional progression of Peshkar\, Kayda\, Rela\, Gat and Tukda. Through rhythm\, composition and improvisation\, the two presentations create an evening where thought becomes swara\, silence becomes sound\, and rhythm becomes expression. \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nAn Exploration of Alap\, Rhythm and Musical Expression\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeZVgYUVk5j_Uz_a90Cw9jahehgvLyZDPRwph7Ivhr6zwcPZg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: A. Mandakini\, Kaustuv Swain\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/swar-soch-laya/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail-5.jpg
