SUMMARY:Tiger Man\, Burning Bright!
DESCRIPTION: \nCan the recovery of a single species hold the key to saving creatures across an entire continent? \nBased on Tiger Memories: My Life in Wildlife Conservation by K. Ullas Karanth\, this panel discussion traces the history and social context of tiger conservation in India and Asia over the past six decades. The conversation illustrates the centrality of rigorous wildlife science to effective conservation\, combining top-down and bottom-up approaches from field biology and statistical ecology\, and explores the future prospects for tigers and wild nature in a wider socio-environmental context. \nCoauthored with naturalist Joshua Mathew and published by Penguin Random House India\, the book illustrates Karanth’s wildlife adventures\, pioneering research\, and passionate battles to save big cats and wild nature. It traces his long career studying and conserving wild tigers\, from exploring the forests of Karnataka’s Malenad as a teenager to becoming one of the world’s leading wildlife biologists. \nPresented by: \n      \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nFighting to Bring Back Asia’s Big Cats\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScJ0H5Dik-OLySNFZmnjwg_KDQyu6Z2x1jWcHX29sBrmoIjtg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: K. Ullas Karanth\, K. VijayRaghavan\,  P. J. Dilip Kumar\, Krithi K. Karanth\, Narayan Ramachandran\, Joshua Mathew\, Praveen Bhargav\, Karthik Venkatesh\n*Event Categories*: Biography\, Books\, Wildlife
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/tiger-man-burning-bright/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Biography,Books,Wildlife
