SUMMARY:The Story We Think We Know
DESCRIPTION:The Undocumented is a work of narrative non-fiction that follows a Bangladeshi family who crossed into India without papers in 2009\, and the life they built since. This conversation\, based on the book\, explore migration: why people leave\, what they encounter on arrival\, and what it means to build a life where your presence can be questioned. The panel will also discuss the invisible work of telling someone else’s story. \nAmid love\, survival\, loss\, and the constant uncertainty of being undocumented\, the book looks past the labels to uncover the lives underneath; beyond the politics of migration to the histories\, routines\, and relationships that make a place home. \nVenue: Library\n\n\nBangladeshi Migrants in India\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfGbZ_v9yWTzbemC2jS19yNQDEp4ykl0GAbDT0IRHpLcETCZA/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Nidhi Dugar Kundalia\, Srikar Raghavan\, Aditi Surie\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Nonfiction\, Politics\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-story-we-think-we-know/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Nonfiction,Politics,Society
