SUMMARY:In-Sight: An Insider’s View into My Choreographies
DESCRIPTION:\nMadhavi Mudgal will explore her journey of finding possibilities within the Odissi framework to expand its boundaries. As a firm believer in our classical traditions\, and having been an active participant in the restructuring of the form by her guru\, Kelucharan Mohapatra\, she has choreographed several solo and group compositions over the last 45 years. This presentation will explore the ideas behind some of these compositions. \nThis is the first edition of ‘Dance – The Creative Process’ a lecture demonstration series presented by Kalavaahini in association with BIC\, curated by Malavika Sarukkai. The series invites audiences into the intimate spaces of different dance forms across India\, exploring the imaginative thinking and artistic choices of some of their most accomplished exponents. The event is managed by Shreya Nagarajan Singh Arts Development Consultancy. \nImage Credits\nThumbnail\, Header\, Poster and Backdrop: Photos of Madhavi Mudgal and disciples by Ajay Lal.\nBiography photo by Unnikrishnan. \nIn collaboration with: \n \n\n\nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nDance – The Creative Process\nA Lecture Demonstration Series\nRSVPs open on Sun\, Sep 13 at 6pm.\n*Performers*: Madhavi Mudgal & Disciples\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Dance\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/in-sight-an-insiders-view-into-my-choreographies/
